---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service — Chekpoint" variant="centered">
  <div class="legal-page">
    <div class="legal-header">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Chekpoint</a>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="effective-date">Effective: January 1, 2025</p>
    </div>

    <div class="legal-body">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
        <p>By accessing or using Chekpoint ("the Service"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service. If you do not agree to these terms, please do not use the Service.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Description of Service</h2>
        <p>Chekpoint is a game review platform that allows users to write and share reviews of video games, follow other reviewers, and discover new games. Game data is provided by IGDB.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. User Accounts</h2>
        <p>You must create an account to post reviews and interact with other users. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activity under your account. You must provide accurate information when creating your account.</p>
        <p>You must be at least 13 years of age to use the Service. By creating an account, you represent that you meet this requirement.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. User Content</h2>
        <p>You retain ownership of content you post ("User Content"). By posting User Content, you grant Chekpoint a non-exclusive, royalty-free, worldwide license to display and distribute that content as part of operating the Service.</p>
        <p>You are solely responsible for your User Content. You agree not to post content that:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Is unlawful, harassing, defamatory, or abusive</li>
          <li>Infringes any third-party intellectual property rights</li>
          <li>Contains spam, malware, or deceptive content</li>
          <li>Violates the privacy of others</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We reserve the right to remove User Content that violates these terms at our sole discretion.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Prohibited Conduct</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Use the Service for any unlawful purpose</li>
          <li>Impersonate any person or entity</li>
          <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any part of the Service</li>
          <li>Scrape or crawl the Service without permission</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Service or its servers</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>The Chekpoint name, logo, and the Service's design and code are the property of Chekpoint. Game data, cover images, and related metadata are provided by IGDB and are subject to their respective terms. You may not use our intellectual property without our prior written consent.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>The Service is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind, either express or implied. We do not guarantee that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or free of harmful components. Reviews and opinions expressed by users are their own and do not represent the views of Chekpoint.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the fullest extent permitted by law, Chekpoint shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages arising from your use of the Service.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. Termination</h2>
        <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate your account at any time for violation of these terms or for any other reason at our discretion. You may delete your account at any time by contacting us.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Changes to Terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these Terms of Service from time to time. Continued use of the Service after changes are posted constitutes acceptance of the revised terms. We will note the effective date of the current version at the top of this page.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>If you have questions about these terms, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--text-primary); }

  h1 {
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .effective-date {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .legal-body {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 36px 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 28px;
  }

  section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }

  h2 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  p, li {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  a { color: var(--accent); }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .legal-body { padding: 24px 20px; }
    h1 { font-size: 26px; }
  }
</style>
